{
  "schema": "aman-release-review-fixes-validation/v1",
  "issue": 887,
  "fixes": [
    "Revalidate future EATs against fresh readiness and propagate postponement in the accepted stream order. Due EATs remain fixed and report readiness conflicts.",
    "Validate accepted reservation timing independently of the optional newly computed HoldingPlan; preserve the accepted EAT/journey and degrade additional intake when it cannot meet its slot.",
    "Evaluate rate/wake entry spacing at the actual candidate release time, reevaluating at rate boundaries; use observed release time when it is later than the offered EAT."
  ],
  "checks": {
    "backend": "Full go run ./internal/testing/testdb ./... passed",
    "focused": "go test ./internal/aman/operational ./internal/aman/release passed",
    "diff": "git diff --check passed"
  },
  "regressions": [
    "Fresh holding arrival moves after a future EAT; an independent feeder remains able to release.",
    "The same readiness slip with a due EAT preserves the target and blocks additional advancement.",
    "HoldingPlan disappears because longer transit cannot fit the slot, with both a retained holding-release basis and raw hold-fix timing.",
    "Current 30/hour versus a scheduled future increase to 60/hour retains two-minute approach entry spacing despite legal one-minute future landing spacing.",
    "Candidate crossing a rate increase/decrease is recalculated at that boundary.",
    "Postponement propagates through existing future offers even when the adapter has already retimed the leader.",
    "An existing future head can advance without being constrained by its own later followers.",
    "Observed release later than EAT is used for following entry spacing."
  ],
